==Enemy==
The bearbershop quintet, now in color! Compared to Bears Be Bare, they are slower, have fewer knockbacks and do less damage with each attack, but don't let that fool you into thinking they're harmless. They can Knockback, Freeze, Slow, Weaken, and/or Warp any unit in their large attack range, and thanks to their multi-hit ability, they have three separate chances for all of these status effects. While still not much of a threat by themselves, they can easily cripple your units (or remove them from the field entirely), allowing other enemies to advance unimpeded.

==Strategy==
Their greatest weakness is the number of traits they have, giving the player no shortage of units that can deal effective damage or put status effects on them, assuming they can get into range. Note that one of their traits is Alien, meaning that if you don't have any [[Anti-unstarred Alien Treasures]], their base health and damage jump to a insane '''350k health''' and 8,400 damage, so you should get as many of the Treasures as possible.

When they appear later on in Zero Legends, their high buffs could end up making them a much bigger threat then they need to be, as they'll be around longer to apply more debuffs. While they don't burrow nor revive, the [[Ototo Corps#Holy Blast|Holy Blast]] can still shave off a good chunk of their health pool and freeze them for a moment.

