==Trivia==
*In the [[Media:Eve l 015 en.png|event poster]] for [[Bears Be Back (Monthly Event)|Bears Be Back]], this enemy is referred to as Variety Bears, which was the only name they had until they were added to the [[Enemy Guide]] in [[Version 13.3 Update|Version 13.3]].
*Their Japanese name, Rainbow Bear Talk, is a reference to the comedy-focused talk show ''[[:wikipedia:Ametalk!|Ametalk!]]'', which has a rainbow as its logo. The Bears Be Back event poster even has a rainbow that looks exactly like the one in Ametalk's logo, but with only warm colors.
*Each one bears resemblances to a different member of a Japanese comedy duo:
**Red = [[wikipedia:ja:カズレーザー|Kaneko "KAZLASER" Kazunori]] of [[wikipedia:ja:メイプル超合金|Maple Chogōkin]] (same hairstyle and hair color, wears red)
**Dark = [https://mydramalist.com/people/66303-miyazon Daiko "Miyazon" Miyazono] of [[wikipedia:ja:ANZEN漫才|Anzen Manzai]] (same guitar, hairstyle and hair color)
**Angel = [https://profile.yoshimoto.co.jp/talent/detail?id=5087 Seiya Ishikawa] of [[wikipedia:ja:霜降り明星|Shimofuri Myojo]] (same necktie, wears a white suit)
**Alien = [https://newsatcl-pctr.c.yimg.jp/t/iwiz-yn/rpr/nakanishimasao/00102853/image04.jpeg?exp=10800 Kazuhiro Unagi] of [[wikipedia:ja:銀シャリ (お笑い)|Ginshari]] (same hairstyle, hair color, suit and tie)
**Zombie = [[wikipedia:ja:安藤なつ|Natsu Ando]] of Maple Chogōkin (chubby, same glasses and hair color, similar hairstyle, wears purple)
***This is alluded to by the Japanese stage names in [[Bears be Bare (Monthly Event)|Bears be Bare]] and [[Bears Be Back (Monthly Event)|Bears Be Back]], most of which are related to comedy.
***This also makes them the character with the most [[Pop Culture References|references]].
*If one looks very closely, they can see that during their attack animation, the guitar stays in the Miyazon-Bear's paw even though it has no opposable thumbs.
*They have the most traits of any enemy, only lacking the [[:Category:Traitless Enemies|Traitless]], [[:Category:Metal Enemies|Metal]], [[:Category:Aku Enemies|Aku]] and [[:Category:Relic Enemies|Relic]] traits.
*They are the only Angel enemy to also be Floating, contradicting [[Angel Fanboy]]'s message of "<span style="color:#ed222d">'''Angel Alert!'''</span> '''Angels ignore anti-Floating attacks!'''".
*They and [[Johnnyleon]] are the only Zombie enemies not to revive.
**Despite their inability to revive, the [[:Category:Zombie Killer Cats|Zombie Killer]] sound and graphic will play if they are defeated by a cat with that ability.
*Bears Be Back, [[Gorilliam]], [[Satan Claus]] and [[Commander Ostromeda]] are the only [[:Category:Unstarred Alien Enemies|unstarred Aliens]] with the Warp ability.
**Commander Ostromeda is the only one to have a description and the only one who was not introduced in a Lucky Ticket G event.
*Interestingly enough, the [[Ursamajor]] and [[Cadaver Bear]] both lack distinguishing features of the enemies they represent. Kazuhiro-Bear doesn't have armor plating on its head and shoulders, and is missing a tail; Natsu-Bear lacks any stitches around its body, along with not having the iconic bolt piercing through its head.

